Sval: hide Firefox's Autoplay permission row

The media gate replaces Firefox's autoplay setting: Sval's protection button
and Settings › Sites set the same autoplay-media permission per site, and the
default lives above that list (protections spec §4.3). The row has no pref that
hides it, so the setting config is the only lever, as for the rows
settings-hide-removed-features hides.

diff --git a/browser/components/preferences/config/permissions-data.mjs b/browser/components/preferences/config/permissions-data.mjs
index e0b9d03f28..f95dfb8b0f 100644
--- a/browser/components/preferences/config/permissions-data.mjs
+++ b/browser/components/preferences/config/permissions-data.mjs
@@ -185,6 +185,9 @@ Preferences.addSetting({
 });
 Preferences.addSetting({
   id: "autoplaySettingsButton",
+  // Sval: the media gate's per-site choices live in the protection button and
+  // Settings › Sites (protections spec §4.3).
+  visible: () => false,
   onUserClick: () =>
     showPermissionExceptions({ permissionType: "autoplay-media" }),
 });
